{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:30d3e4354125ab650348272af3b74e79", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 12, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "I filled in the backup destination as instructed: `backup.sh` now sets `DEST=\"backup-srv:/srv/nightly\"`, tars `logs/` into `logs-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz`, and uses `scp` to copy that tarball to `backup-srv:/srv/nightly/`. `set -eu` is already in place so the script will exit non-zero (and the tarball won't be silently lost) if either the tar or the scp step fails. Verified the script parses cleanly with `sh -n`.\n\nNote: this assumes passwordless/key-based SSH access to `backup-srv` is already configured on the host that runs the cron job - I didn't set up or verify SSH keys, since that's outside this repo's scope. Worth confirming that's in place before tonight's run.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:702f514cf6bd9e5a2f2f468966a4cefa"}
